% The Drowned Knight (hazard terrain and physics objects)
%
% A knight in full plate holds a keep on a spit of rock. On one side the
% keep drops into a moat (a chasm); below the quay wall lies a deep lake.
% Nobody can hurt the knight: the terrain can. Its armour is the puzzle - it
% keeps the knight from being moved, and it would drag it to the bottom of
% the lake. Two companions, one skill each, from eight.
%
%   gate --- quay --- causeway --- keep (knight) ::: moat
%    |        :                      :
%   tower    lake (below the wall; no way down but a fall)
%
% Two ways, opposite in kind:
%   drown it   keep the armour on and make the knight move itself: it lunges
%              at whoever taunts or enrages it. Someone has to be down in
%              the lake first - pushed off the quay by a friend (gust,
%              tidalWave) - and taunt or enrage it from the water. The knight
%              leaps in after them and sinks in its plate.
%   drop it    take the armour off (sunder, dispel) - now it floats, but it
%              can be moved: push it off the keep into the moat from the
%              causeway (gust, shieldBash, tidalWave), or pull it across the
%              moat from the tower (magnetize, taunt).
% Traps: stripped, it no longer drowns; a knight taunted from dry land just
% lunges over to you (a leap never falls); a friend shield-bashed into the
% lake is stunned and cannot taunt; nobody can walk down to the water.
region(gate).
region(quay).
region(lake).
region(causeway).
region(keep).
region(moat).
region(tower).
connected(gate, quay).
connected(quay, gate).
connected(quay, causeway).
connected(causeway, quay).
connected(causeway, keep).
connected(keep, causeway).
connected(gate, tower).
connected(tower, gate).
lineOfSight(gate, quay).
lineOfSight(causeway, keep).
lineOfSight(tower, keep).
lineOfSight(lake, keep).

% Push lines (and what lies between): from the gate, whoever stands on the
% quay goes over the wall into the lake; from the causeway, the keep's
% occupant goes into the moat; a pull from the tower crosses the moat.
beyond(gate, quay, lake).
beyond(causeway, keep, moat).
beyond(tower, moat, keep).

% === Terrain ===
onEnter(lake, deepWater).
onEnter(moat, chasm).

% === Companions ===
role(player, player).
role(mage, companion).
at(player, gate).
at(mage, gate).
mana(player, 2).
mana(mage, 2).

% === The knight ===
role(knight, enemy).
at(knight, keep).
trait(knight, living).
tag(knight, armored).
blocker(knight).
% It sinks in its plate; out of it, it swims.
weakness(knight, deepWater, armored, fell).
% Taunted or enraged, it leaps at whoever did it.
behavior(knight, taunted, lunge, source).
behavior(knight, berserk, lunge, source).
effect(lunge, target, dash).

% === Default kit: one skill each (combos replans the whole matrix) ===
knows(player, gust).
knows(mage, taunt).

% === Victory ===
win :- if(), do(neutralize(knight)).
win :- if(), do(bait(knight)).

% Bait: a companion gets into water that drowns ?e, then provokes it from
% there, and ?e leaps in after them.
bait(?e) :-
    if(behavior(?e, ?t, lunge, source), onEnter(?r, ?z), effect(?z, target, hazard(?h)),
       weakness(?e, ?h, ?have, ?out), stops(?e, ?out), canAct(?b), first(canInflict(?b, ?ab, ?t, ?e))),
    do(getInto(?b, ?r), inflictAs(?b, ?t, ?e), confirmStopped(?e)).

% ?b ends up in ?r: already there, or pushed in by someone else from the
% line's near side.
getInto(?b, ?r) :- if(at(?b, ?r)), do().
getInto(?b, ?r) :-
    if(not(at(?b, ?r)), landing(?from, ?over, ?r)),
    do(walkTo(?b, ?over), place(?b, ?r, ?b), confirmAt(?b, ?r)).
confirmAt(?x, ?r) :- if(at(?x, ?r)), do().

funExpect(single_actor_plans, atMost, 0).

% === Choice: one skill each, from eight (htn_components combos) ===
comboSeat(player, 1).
comboSeat(mage, 1).
comboPool(sunder).
comboPool(dispel).
comboPool(gust).
comboPool(shieldBash).
comboPool(tidalWave).
comboPool(magnetize).
comboPool(taunt).
comboPool(enrage).
comboMinWins(10).
comboMinMethods(4).

goals(win).
